      "title": "Corona charging and collection",
      "description": "A high negative DC voltage on the discharge wires ionises the gas (corona). Dust particles pick up charge and drift to the earthed plates, where they collect. Periodic rapping drops the dust layer into the hoppers. ESPs reach very high efficiencies (typically > 99.5 %); dust resistivity, gas temperature and flow distribution govern performance. Recovered alumina is returned to product.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
